{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IntervalRotate"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.length_garnir_eq_add_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.length_garnir_eq_add_iff","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirTableau.lean#L144-L160","doc":"**The length half of Mathas 3.13, against the actual Garnir tableau.**\n\nFor `t = w • g_{ij}`, length is additive exactly when `w` undoes none of\n`g_{ij}`'s inversions.  Both sides are now concrete: the right-hand side is a\ncontainment between inversion sets of explicit permutations, with no lengths and\nno reduced words in it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.not_isDescentNode_refTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.not_isDescentNode_refTab","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirTableau.lean#L128-L140","doc":"The reference tableau has no descent node: it is row-superstandard, so labels\nincrease down every column. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.IsDescentNode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.IsDescentNode","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirTableau.lean#L118-L126","doc":"`(i, j)` is a **descent node** of `t`: `(i+1, j)` is a cell and the label in\n`(i, j)` exceeds the label in `(i+1, j)` — i.e. column-strictness fails there.\n\nA standard tableau has none; Mathas 3.13 picks its Garnir tableau at one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnirTab_ne_refTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnirTab_ne_refTab","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirTableau.lean#L108-L114","doc":"Hence the Garnir tableau differs from the reference tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnirPerm_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnirPerm_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirTableau.lean#L93-L106","doc":"**`g_{ij}` genuinely moves something**: the Garnir permutation is never `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnir_shift_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnir_shift_lt","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirTableau.lean#L87-L91","doc":"The rotation amount is a proper shift: `0 < j + 1 < rowLen μ i + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnirPerm_eq_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnirPerm_eq_self","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirTableau.lean#L73-L78","doc":"Labels outside the block are untouched by `g_{ij}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.dOf_garnirTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.dOf_garnirTab","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirTableau.lean#L68-L71","doc":"`d(g_{ij})` is the Garnir permutation — the two definitions agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnirTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnirTab","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirTableau.lean#L63-L66","doc":"**The Garnir tableau** `g_{ij}`, as the reference tableau moved by that rotation.\nBijectivity is inherited from `intervalRotate`; nothing is proved surjective here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnirPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnirPerm","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirTableau.lean#L58-L61","doc":"**The Garnir permutation** `d(g_{ij})`: rotate the label block\n`[rowPrefix μ i + j, rowPrefix μ (i+1) + j]` by `j+1`, fixing every other label. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnir_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau.garnir_bound","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirTableau.lean#L44-L56","doc":"The rotated block `[a, a+m)` fits inside the labels: `a + m = b + 1 ≤ n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}